//? Title: Integrated gradients:visible midpoint paths and completeness controls
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An endpoint derivative may miss a feature after a classifier score saturates. Integrate ordinary fixed-target derivatives from an explicit baseline to each genuine MNIST image,then check every numerical completeness residual and baseline,target and initialization control.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/integrated_gradients.cpp`.

> The method

For a fixed raw scoreFand baseline x0,straight-line attribution integrates each ordinary coordinate derivative along the path:

$$ IG_i=(x_i-x_{0i})\int_0^1\partial_iF(x_0+\alpha(x-x_0))\,d\alpha,\qquad\sum_iIG_i=F(x)-F(x_0). $$
\alttext(Integrated attribution multiplies the input-baseline coordinate difference by the path-integrated ordinary derivative;the ideal sum equals the endpoint score change.)

The equality follows by the chain rule and fundamental theorem along the path,including piecewise-linear regions almost everywhere. Finite midpoint quadrature approximates the integral;the baseline and target define the attribution question. All numerical preprocessing,derivatives,integrals,checks and plots remain tensors;no optimizer is needed for this frozen-model numerical integration.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/integrated_gradients_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/integrated_gradients_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/integrated_gradients_concept.tikz > build/integrated_gradients_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/integrated_gradients_concept.svg build/integrated_gradients_concept.dvi > build/integrated_gradients_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
