\caption(Every actual case/control completeness check uses its own endpoint score change and fixed tolerance. Ratios below1verify the declared finite-quadrature accuracy;they do not prove explanation quality or monotonic refinement.)
\alttext(Every actual case/control completeness check uses its own endpoint score change and fixed tolerance. Ratios below1verify the declared finite-quadrature accuracy;they do not prove explanation quality or monotonic refinement.)


> Conclusion

Saturation and dummy-coordinate fixtures make the mechanism hand-checkable. Genuine fixed-weight MNIST paths retain every sampled derivative and all completeness errors;baseline,target and initialization changes alter the question and the result. Numerical completeness is an integration check,not causal validation.

> References

- [Sundararajan,Taly and Yan(2017),Axiomatic Attribution for Deep Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01365).
